\h Psalms
\toc1 Psalms
\mt1 Psalms
\c 23
\s1 Psalm 23
\d A psalm of David.
\q1
\v 1 The \nd Lord\nd* is my shepherd;
\q2 I have all that I need.
\q1
\v 2 He lets me rest in green meadows;
\q2 he leads me beside peaceful streams.
\q2 
\v 3 He renews my strength.
\q1 He guides me along right paths,
\q2 bringing honor to his name.
\q1
\v 4 Even when I walk
\q2 through the darkest valley,\f + \ft Or the dark valley of death.\f*
\q1 I will not be afraid,
\q2 for you are close beside me.
\q1 Your rod and your staff
\q2 protect and comfort me.
\q1
\v 5 You prepare a feast for me
\q2 in the presence of my enemies.
\q1 You honor me by anointing my head with oil.
\q2 My cup overflows with blessings.
\q1
\v 6 Surely your goodness and unfailing love will pursue me
\q2 all the days of my life,
\q1 and I will live in the house of the \nd Lord\nd*
\q2 forever.
